@* Select's Overview, written by hand after TextField's: options from an enum or a list, rich
   options where the browser allows, a required select with a placeholder previewed in each mode,
   sizes and states, and what to use when a change should filter the page. Accessibility and See
   also come from the doc comment. *@

<TextBlock>A select is a field with a list of options, one of which the user picks, for short lists. It's a native select, so it posts with the form, <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor> too.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>For a long list, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/combobox">Combobox</Anchor>, which the user types to filter. For several choices, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/multi-select">MultiSelect</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Options</Heading>
<TextBlock>Bound to an enum, a Select shows each value as an option, named by its <Code>[Display(Name)]</Code>. For any other type, pass <Code>Items</Code>, and set <Code>ItemText</Code> for how each option reads. To add an empty first option, set <Code>Placeholder</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="select-usage" />
<TextBlock>The label and required mark come from the model, as they do for a <Anchor Href="docs/components/text-field">TextField</Anchor>. The label is the <Code>[Display(Name)]</Code>, or the property name in words, and <Code>[Required]</Code> adds the mark. To replace the label, set <Code>Label</Code>; to add help under the field, set <Code>Hint</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Rich options</Heading>
<TextBlock>Rich options show markup in each option, such as an icon and a price. Set <Code>ItemTemplate</Code>. Text with the class <Code>ib-option-hint</Code> shows in the list but not in the closed field.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="select-rich" />
<TextBlock>The markup shows in browsers that support the customizable select. In other browsers, IzzyBlazor's script shows <Code>ItemText</Code> in the browser's own list, so set both. With JavaScript off, those browsers show the markup's text run together.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Groups</Heading>
<TextBlock>To list the options under headings, set <Code>ItemGroup</Code> to each option's group, such as a time zone's region. An enum's options group by their <Code>[Display(GroupName)]</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="select-groups" />
<TextBlock>The groups show in the order they first appear, with options that have no group first. They're the browser's own option groups, so they show with JavaScript off too.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Required, with a placeholder</Heading>
<TextBlock>A select can start with nothing chosen and require a choice. Bind a nullable property with <Code>[Required]</Code>, and set a <Code>Placeholder</Code>. Nothing is chosen until the user picks an option, and the placeholder can't be picked again.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="select-required" />

<Heading Level="2">Sizes, read-only and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>To line the field up with buttons and other fields, set <Code>Size</Code>. For a value the user can see but not change, set <Code>ReadOnly</Code>; it still posts. For a value that doesn't post, set <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="select-states" />
<TextBlock>HTML has no read-only select: a read-only Select shows its choice in a read-only text field and posts it from a hidden input. Before trusting a posted value, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#values-a-form-post-can-change">Values a form post can change</Anchor>. Before saving a disabled value from a form post, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Filtering a page</Heading>
<TextBlock>A select doesn't post when it changes. To filter a list as soon as the user picks an option, use a <Code>FilterSelect</Code> in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/filter-form">FilterForm</Anchor>. It applies on change with IzzyBlazor's script, and shows an Apply button with JavaScript off.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Filter</Code>
<TextBlock>On interactive pages, <Code>@@bind-Value:after</Code> runs C# after each change.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Filter = """
        @* Any page: sets ?status= *@
        <FilterForm>
            <FilterSelect Name="status" Label="Status" EnumType="typeof(OrderStatus)" />
        </FilterForm>

        @* Interactive page: C# after each change. *@
        <Select @bind-Value="Model!.Status" @bind-Value:after="ReloadAsync" />
        """;
}
